{"text": " You wake up in 1610 beside the River Thames. It is a misty December morning and the sun hangs low and dim. Thomas Harriet points a telescope at it and draws what he sees. Do not try this, looking at the sun can blind you. Did you know that the first telescope drawing of sunspots was made not by Galileo, but by this Englishman and he never published it? Two years later in Florence, Galileo watched the spots drift across the sun day after day. Arrival said they were tiny planets passing in front. Galileo disagreed. The spots were on the sun itself and the sun was turning. In 1613 he published his letters. The perfect heavenly body had blemishes. For most people, the day still runs on daylight alone. But for a few, the sun has become something you can measure. And soon one simple glass prism will break that light apart.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.68, "text": " You wake up in 1610 beside the River Thames.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 3165, 3279, 15726, 264, 8640, 334, 1632, 13, 50516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13556603022984096, "compression_ratio": 1.6123188405797102, "no_speech_prob": 0.00946716871112585, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.12, "probability": 0.6179913878440857}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.3, "probability": 0.9920215010643005}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.3, "end": 0.5, "probability": 0.9976813793182373}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.5, "end": 0.64, "probability": 0.9824510216712952}, {"word": " 1610", "start": 0.64, "end": 1.5, "probability": 0.944356381893158}, {"word": " beside", "start": 1.5, "end": 1.9, "probability": 0.7446319460868835}, {"word": " the", "start": 1.9, "end": 2.12, "probability": 0.9712291359901428}, {"word": " River", "start": 2.12, "end": 2.3, "probability": 0.6294453144073486}, {"word": " Thames.", "start": 2.3, "end": 2.68, "probability": 0.8685987889766693}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 3.08, "end": 4.72, "text": " It is a misty 